{"author":{"id":"6033ad3a62469493b79b19fe4fb66aa96b5a224ed38b3533d8d3f1b8cf68be03"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1794013987,"nonce":"QpWOfiMNLY62FdBq2BWZK0JiRds=","target":"1b66ed074540c93d637d4ad99ce07a8d4487d84d3bccb5bf0ab606cc76a47644","message":"Part of epic nov-kot. Rewrite of rakelib/3_roles_files.rake and raw/prompts/extract_roles.txt.\n\n## Input\n\nThe distinct `actor` strings of the process (from `_user_stories_src.jsonl`), the opis.md as context, and grouped_participants.json (now with P-03.2 «Внешний участник»).\n\n## Output\n\n- `{id}_roles.jsonl` in the May schema: `role_id` ({pid}-R-NN), `role`, `description`, `participant` {code, name}. doc tables (2) and (3) stay unchanged.\n- `{id}_actor_roles.jsonl`: `actor` (verbatim) → `role_ids`.\n\n## Rules, as in the approved May KOT\n\n- Split a compound actor into atomic singular roles, one participant each. May split «Председатель суда, заместитель председателя суда, председатель судебного состава» in ТБП27 into three roles and «Судья/Помощник судьи» in ТБП19 into two.\n- A parenthesis clarifies the head noun: ТБП7 «Заявитель (ЛУВД, …)» became «Заявитель».\n- No group roles («Суд», «ЛУВД»); no «Система».\n- OBP actors are court staff unless they are outside organisations (Госархив, Подрядчик, Поставщик, Кандидат → P-03.2).\n- The LLM writes the description of each role for this process (decision 3).\n\n## Validation\n\nEvery actor maps to at least one role, every role is used, and every participant code is valid. A new task `check:role_participants` (no LLM) lists role names mapped to different participants in different processes.\n\n## Your run\n\nTry one process first, for example `rake work/ba/TBP27/TBP27_roles.jsonl`, then `rake roles` (LLM, 231 calls), then `rake check:role_participants`. Check: no .err, and the consistency report in out/check_role_participants.jsonl.","files":null}]}